// comment processor at -527,-885 503x671: "===============\nDOCUMENTATION\n===============\n\nThis sprite processes the visible geometry (both static and dynamic), as well as the camera constraints.\n\nFor static geometry (in the tris and verts lists), vertices get moved and projected and placed in both the projected AND cam space lists. There are 2 lists to enable z clipping to occur for the tri filler.\n\nThis sprite also handles geometry that can move (dynamic). This includes doors and trains.\n\nA separate list is used to indicate where in the tris and verts list they are located. It is only in this sprite where they are adjusted for position. Dynamic geometry remains loaded at all times alongside the static geometry."
// comment processor at 3087,-854 200x200 minimized: "debug"
// comment processor at -1408.111111111111,100.51851851851852 419.25927734375x180.74075317382812: "optimisation used: make the search only happen once, cache the result for later verts"
// comment processor at -856.8043975830078,2841 200x200 minimized: "must be set to 1 (custom implementation of dx, dy, dz)"
// comment processor at -794.0370370370371,3243.8888888888887 247.4073486328125x127.40740966796875: "y=a\\cdot\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\operatorname{abs}\\left(x\\right)\\cdot s\\right)\\cdot x^{2}"
// comment obj_loader at 315.6944444444444,233.33333333333633 200x200: "contains the entirety of the game"
// comment obj_loader at -386.22222222222194,1835.7777777777778 200x200 minimized: "NOTE: obj file orientation"
// comment obj_loader at 1803.3333333333333,4661.333333333334 200x200 minimized: "buffer for height detection"
// comment obj_loader at 2804.333333333333,5417.333333333334 200x200 minimized: "3 is arbitrary buffer"
// comment obj_loader at -423,12 512x670: "===============\nDOCUMENTATION\n===============\n\nThis sprite loads the scene.\n\nWORLD.obj is slow to access so is cached into the lists starting with v, the cleaned file list, and the names (which point to the cleaned file and not the original file).\n\nWhen a region gets loaded, the obj directory list is checked and any objects that contain the correct region name are loaded.\n\nThe name is separated into a hierarchy: \n[region name],[FL/VZ/DY],[room or object subname(if not FL)],[BB (if vz)]\nFL is floor\nVZ is static visible geometry\nDY is dynamic geometry (things that can be moved such as doors)\nBB is bounding box and is used by static geometry for only rendering when unoccluded.\n\nThere is only 1 floor per region, which is fine as it's not slow and it makes the wall generation simple.\n\nWalls are generated by finding exposed edges (edges that are not shared by 2 adjacent triangles). A line segment is added. Actually, the walls are geometrically stadia (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stadium_(geometry)) extruded along the Z axis.\n\nRegions are split into rooms for improved performance. Rooms are separate objects. The default main room which is always visible will not have a subname, it will just be [region name]_VZ. Any other room must be accompanied by a bounding box to be visible. The bounding box is calculated by the bounds of the tris of the object and can be of whatever you want. I use rectangular prisms. \nDynamic geometry does not need a bounding box, it will always be visible. A bounding box of size infinity is created automatically.\n"
// comment obj_loader at 4394,3055 262x121: "bounding sphere not used?"
// comment obj_loader at 9045.703703703704,1540.7037037037037 200x200: "1122534\n1067623\n1051196\n996585\n893517"
// comment img_loader at 286.9629629629631,601.037037037037 195x97: "Edges aren't scannable??"
// comment img_loader at 1244,1675 200x200 minimized: "NOTE: obj file orientation"
// comment img_loader at 624.62962962963,410.44444444444446 200x200 minimized: "keeps track of what is loaded"
// comment img_loader at 3842,36 656x838: "===============\nDOCUMENTATION\n===============\n\nscanner by @Geotale\nhttps://scratch.mit.edu/projects/643721525/\nremixed by @awesome-llama (for the purposes of modularisation)\nhttps://scratch.mit.edu/projects/840839772\n\n\nThere are many textures used in the game. Each object has been made to have exactly 1 material and this is stored in the obj file. Each material has one texture. This project doesn't properly differentiate the two so 'material name' = 'texture name' here. \n\nSince only the pod is accessible at the start of the game, the full-res textures have been included and are separately stored in the pod texture variable. They are loaded in this sprite too and bypass the compressed textures list.\n\n"
