// comment tags at -1155,-256 562x569: "===============\nDOCUMENTATION\n===============\n\nThis sprite handles tags (things you can look at and read or interact with).\nThere are 3 kinds - text, document, function.\n\ntext: readable on screen, e.g. a sign\ndocument: interact with it to show something on the screen, e.g. a map or button panel\nfunction: directly triggers something when interacted with, e.g. a door open button.\n\nTags are placed in 3D space. They have a normal direction which prevents them from being viewed from behind, say, through walls. Range to appear is by default 2 metres. All interactable tags can be done so within 1.5 metres. Display range can be set with the custom block.\n\nID is used to differentiate tags. It is not used for text as it's not needed but the other types do because they trigger other scripts.\n\nA single sound effect can be added to a tag and will play if interacted with.\n\nTags are static and are only loaded when the region is loaded. Any time a tag needs to be updated, the load tags script must be run to regenerate the tags."
// comment tags at 3222,2228 200x200: "white diamonds\ncoloured dots"
// comment game_states at -1593,179 516x541: "===============\nDOCUMENTATION\n===============\n\nThis sprite handles game states.\n\nGame states are stored in list items and affect things like door positions and items in possession. \nSee the reset game states broadcast for the states that exist.\n\nFunction tags are handled here too. They go through a stack of if-else blocks.\nFunction tags with an ID starting with # are handled as commands where a game state is immediately after, followed by =, followed by the value the state should be set to.\nSetting \"has keycard\" to 1 can be done with \"#has keycard=1\"\n\nThe green flag can soft lock the game due to the wait blocks being reset. A fix has been added to ensure that any attempted change of a game state will see it reset to the old value."
// comment game_states at 772,2859 521x488: "green panel to unlock door\n\nset of switches and toggles need to be correct\n\nlift operation\noff (default), neutral, on\n\nlift power\noff, standby (default), on (requires lift to be on neutral mode)\n\nlift only works when on\n\nlift start-up operation:\n0. unlock door to access controls\n1. set power to OFF or STANDBY\n2. switch operation to NEUTRAL (requires off or standby set before)\n3. switch power to ON (requires neutral set before)\n3. switch operation to ON (requires on set before)\n4. close door (for safety)"
